    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Description\n\nHello, and happy new year! I have a question: is there a way to change how `<Space>` is displayed in `mini.clue`? I noticed that the space is quite wide, and I would prefer to replace it with custom text or a character to make it more compact.  \r\nAdditionally, I would like to change the window title from `<Space>` to custom text. Is this possible? If so, could you guide me on how to configure this?\r\n\r\n![imagen](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dc5de074-381b-4a81-afb5-d877678375a7)\r\nFor example, in `which-key`, as you can see in the screenshot (with the arrows pointing to `<Space>`), the `<Space>` has been replaced with a more compact representation. Can we achieve the same in `mini.clue`?\r\n![imagen](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0257027a-cff9-40e0-89be-98971a8a2193)\r\n",
